-- title:
--   Interpolate Completed Slices From Support Restrict At Height Poly Eq Get Of Mem
-- statement:
--   **Lagrange interpolation recovers each selected completed slice.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `xs` be injective, let `gs` be completed outcomes, and let $\sigma$ satisfy the support and cardinality hypotheses. For every $i\in\sigma$, the interpolation polynomial recovers the selected slice polynomial at its height:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{evalAtHeight}_{xs(i)}\left(\operatorname{interpolateCompletedSlicesFromSupport}(\mathrm{params},xs,gs,\sigma,\ldots).\operatorname{poly}\right)=\left((gs(i)).\operatorname{get}(\ldots)\right).\operatorname{poly}.
--   $$
--
--   Injectivity makes the interpolation nodes distinct, while the support hypotheses ensure that all selected inputs are genuine completed slices.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.interpolateCompletedSlicesFromSupport_restrictAtHeight_poly_eq_get_of_mem`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
